# Peios glibc patch series — applied in order by pekit during source
# materialisation ([source].patches in pekit.toml).
#
# The bar for production changes here stays high: every patch is a rebase on
# every glibc release, on the most security-critical library on the system.
# The ABI and NSS patches deliberately affect shipped behavior; the final six
# patches are test-harness-only and do not alter shipped objects.
abi/peios-syscalls.patch                 # expose the stable Peios kernel syscall ABI through sys/syscall.h
nss/identity-is-not-configurable.patch   # freeze authority identity/hosts and keep legacy Secure RPC publickey empty
tests/fortify-format-security.patch      # keep intentional -Wno-format tests compatible with workspace -Werror=format-security
tests/unsupported-special-tests.patch    # let policy exclusions cover derived tests-special companions
tests/minimal-native-root.patch          # retain tests in accountless single-ID build roots
tests/fixed-provider-glob-oracle.patch  # host passwd is not the Peios authority; staged provider supplies named-user coverage
tests/latepthread-unbounded-diagnostic.patch  # retain full loader error for long build paths
tests/standalone-spawn-pwd.patch         # spawn tests need a standalone utility when invoked through a differently named symlink
